":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":26,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Evaluation criteria: ① the removal target was chosen ","position":{"start":{"line":26,"column":1},"end":{"line":26,"column":1}},"key":"VtmKqxkWHj"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":26,"column":1},"end":{"line":26,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"on train only","position":{"start":{"line":26,"column":1},"end":{"line":26,"column":1}},"key":"X4oLhmGcTi"}],"key":"TMcz7U5q58"},{"type":"text","value":", ② for a single keyword, report the drop in the AUROC of the test proteins with an interval from the Pfam-group bootstrap, and keep the results extended to several keywords and several features in a separate table, ③ separate and describe the “reconstruction cost” and the “feature-removal effect” by the difference between (ii) and (iii), ④ if the drop is small or absent, describe the possible reasons (information duplicated in other features, superposition, the feature is only correlated with the keyword and the probe does not use it, etc.) and the cases where “there is correlation but no causation” is possible, ⑤ extension (optional): FVU vs the median keyword AUROC for dictionary size {1×, 4×, 8×, 16×} and k ∈ {8, 32, 128}, residue-level activation density, stability across seeds. To do it at layer 6, the intervened activations must be passed again through layers 7–12, and the probe input is layer 12 after that.","position":{"start":{"line":26,"column":1},"end":{"line":26,"column":1}},"key":"pgSXHGofWY"}],"key":"MKmMn3OVLm"}],"key":"EFUSYCGkOJ"}],"key":"soblxsGggZ"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Exercise 5 — Benchmark design document  ","position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"key":"Z4fWCgipJ0"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":